A||||5||johnmac||Rear Suspension Bolt Replacement||||1||
Z||000000||johnmac||10-13-2001||10:17 AM||||My 2 bolts that tighten around the rear ball joints rod need replacement.<P>Can I swap out Grade 8 metric bolts (10mm) for these. A NAPA dealer tells me I need to go to the Pontiac Dealer for replacements.<P>They are to be torqued to 37 Ft-Lbs per the shop manual.<P>Comments please!<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000001||Banzai||10-13-2001||12:34 PM||||Did you replace the ball joints? My new ones came with  bolts. I'm not quite sure but I think the ball joints were only about 19 bucks apiece.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-13-2001||02:25 PM||||I just used regular metric bolts for mine..<P>Shes still running so it must work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnmac||10-13-2001||02:50 PM||||My ball joints were okay once I cleaned them up and replace the grease cups.<P>I tried 1 metric bolt but later inspection revealed the material was too soft as the surface was indented by the ball joint stud.<P>Need to get case hardened mat'l to be safe.<P>Went to the Fort Knox, i.e. Pontiac Dealer and order 2 with nuts for $10.00.<P>Ouch!!<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-13-2001||03:14 PM||||You probably could have gotten more pinch bolts from FWD cars at the local scrap yard but new is better. This is one of those bolts not to take chances with...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||johnmac||10-13-2001||11:42 PM||||A big ten four on that.<P>Don't want the rear suspension collapsing on me while I am cruisin down the highway!<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
